# Textus Knowledge Lake CML Model

> NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> This file is the canonical CML source location for the TKL application model.
> Replace this scaffold with valid current CML syntax after checking the CML/Cozy implementation and existing examples.
> Do not invent unsupported CML syntax.
>
> Design source:
> - docs/notes/application-model.md
> - docs/notes/architecture.md
> - docs/phase/phase-1.md
> - docs/journal/2026-10-02-phase-1-project-local-boundary.md
> - docs/journal/2026-09-23-tkl-core-architecture-consolidation.md
>
> Modeling intent:
> - Model application-level Use Cases separately from execution Workflows.
> - Keep future TKL Use Cases in the application model even when they are outside Phase 1.
> - Phase 1 primary Use Case is "Propose Raw Knowledge Candidate".
> - Phase 1 is project-local: implement TKL preparation/proposal and validate its boundary with local fixtures.
> - Actual TKW receipt, KnowledgeHub Admission, TEAI transport and BoK publication are external follow-up proposals.
> - Manage integration requirements and deliver concrete owner proposals at Phase closure.
> - Derive/associate Application Capabilities where supported by current CML.
> - Use current CML concepts for Use Case Slice / executable specification only if they are actually supported.
>
> Primary application areas:
> 1. Knowledge Acquisition
>    - Propose Raw Knowledge Candidate [Phase 1 primary]
>    - Explore Candidates by Theme
>    - Discover Candidates from New Evidence
>    - Inspect Candidate Evidence
>    - Prepare Against Existing Knowledge Context
>    - Deliver Raw Candidate Proposal [TKL side; local boundary fixture in Phase 1]
>    - Candidate editing/review/approval/Admission belong to TKW.
> 2. Research / Exploration
> 3. Project Awareness
> 4. Content Production
>
> Phase 1 workflow outline:
> Determine Knowledgeization Scope
> -> Resolve Knowledge Resources
> -> Collect Evidence
> -> Normalize Evidence
> -> Create / Resolve KnowledgeProcessingContext
> -> Record External Context Binding
> -> Create ProcessingRun / Fix Input and Existing Information Snapshots
> -> Prepare Knowledge Material
> -> Persist PreparedMaterial
> -> Extract Raw Knowledge Candidate
> -> Compose Candidate Proposal
> -> Present Proposal and Evidence
> -> Export Proposal / Record TKL Boundary Result and Correspondence
> -> Emit External Integration Proposals at Phase Closure
>
> Use repository-owned source/result fixtures, local persistence and simulated boundary results for Phase 1.
> A fixture receipt does not establish TKW deduplication, human approval or actual Admission.
> Do not introduce another project's build/service as a closure dependency or implement its replacement locally.
>
> Important domain concepts to align with the model:
> - KnowledgeResource / provider-independent resource identity
> - Evidence
> - KnowledgeProcessingContext / externalContextBindings
> - ProcessingRun / fixed input manifest and retained-content status
> - Communication Value Objects
> - PreparedMaterial Entity
> - RawCandidateProposal / producer-scoped proposalId
> - Provenance / Lineage
> - TKL proposal/result correlation boundary
>
> Provider-specific Google Workspace / Slack details are implementation mappings,
> not the semantic core of this CML model.
>
