> KNOWLEDGE FEEDBACK NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> Add Knowledge Feedback as a first-class application-use-case group in the native CML model where supported:
> - Synchronize Knowledge Context
> - Project Knowledge to Preparation Workspace
> - Refresh Knowledge Context after Formation
> - Trace Knowledge Formation
>
> Existing acquisition/research/awareness use cases use Existing Knowledge Context when relevant; Phase 1 uses a versioned local baseline fixture.
>
> Model the application loop:
> KnowledgeHub -> TKL KnowledgeProjection -> Preparation -> Raw Candidate -> TKW -> KnowledgeHub.
> This is the future application relationship. Live feedback synchronization is follow-on scope, managed in the integration register.


> KNOWLEDGE PROJECTION SYNC NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> Model the basic Knowledge Feedback synchronization capabilities/use cases where supported:
> - append KnowledgeProjectionDelta for new/update/supersede changes;
> - build/rebuild KnowledgeContextSnapshot from KnowledgeHub canonical current state;
> - publish current snapshot + post-snapshot deltas to preparation workspaces;
> - remove/deactivate obsolete projection context after rebuild.
>
> Principle: append frequently, rebuild periodically.
> Keep full live synchronization outside project-local Phase 1 acceptance.


> GOOGLE WORKSPACE PRIORITY NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> Target Drive folders for production TKL JSON storage and Drive Project for the first external preparation context.
> Phase 1 validates local representations/manual-result fixtures without live Google operations.
> Gemini Notebook is an optional context for preparation/analysis/synthesis/production; exact product/API capabilities need adapter verification.
> Do not introduce Notebook synchronization as a Phase 1 dependency.
